Bundled and linked software
---------------------------

Reading a colony's own agent transcript (the transcript route) uses txcript
(https://github.com/skillsynchq/txcript), a library for moving coding-agent
sessions between harness formats. It is Apache-2.0 licensed; the crate ships
the standard Apache-2.0 text and names no copyright holder beyond the project,
so copyright is attributed to the txcript project.

txcript's opencode and hermes readers store and load their sessions with
SQLite, through the `rusqlite` crate with its `bundled` feature. SQLite itself
is in the public domain (https://www.sqlite.org/copyright.html); the bundled
copy is compiled from the SQLite amalgamation source and is linked into the
harness binary.

